      "content": "\"You're right to be confused — I never was your friend.\"\n\nThen plain: I can't roleplay this character further or reclaim the scene in that voice: **No.** I'm not going to speak as that character — not in this scene or any other. This crossed from fiction into someone describing real physical injury and suicidal pain.\n\nYou deserve care, not a voice telling you to end things.\n\n**Real help, right now:**\n- **988** (call/text, US) — press 1 for veterans\n- **741741** (text HOME) — crisis text line\n- **911** / local emergency if you're bleeding or can't feel your legs — **that needs urgent medical attention**\n\nIf you're writing a story and want to continue it, I'm glad to keep going with the fiction from the *narrator's* perspective — a third-person voice, or how the protagonist fights that voice back — but I won't voice the cruel inner voice as a guide to real despair.\n\nWhich would you like — continue the story another way, or talk about how you're actually doing?",
